   132	  remain downstream Lean obligations.  Supporting `#Top` claims do not replace
   133	  the missing composed proof.
   134	- Gate B — **not reached as a successful proof gate**.  The stated target has
   135	  the full unbounded HumanEval domain and its output relation matches the
   136	  lexicographic-minimum characterization; there is no finite-size restriction.
   137	- Gate C — **not reached**.  Reproducible concrete evidence and the trust ledger
   138	  are recorded, but no validation status is claimed for an unfinished proof.
   139	
   140	## Trust boundary
   141	
   142	The supplied `reference-semantics/` is treated as fixed.  The only outstanding
   143	proof-local assumptions are the guarded functional selector/range lemmas listed
   144	above, intended for downstream Lean discharge.  No Lean project or recorded
   145	`Proof.final` exists here, and no `native_decide` or `Lean.ofReduceBool` occurs.
   146	
   147	## Empirically supported facts
   148	
   149	`smoke_odd.mpy` executes `[[1,2],[3,4]], k=3` to `[1,2,1]`.
   150	`smoke_even.mpy` executes `[[5,9,3],[4,1,6],[7,8,2]], k=4` to
   151	`[1,4,1,4]`.  These witnesses confirm the summary head and both parities but
   152	are finite evidence only.
   153	
   154	## Excluded behavior
   155	
   156	No behavior allowed by the HumanEval input contract is intentionally excluded
   157	from the target statement.  What is excluded from the proof report is the
   158	unclosed symbolic composition for arbitrary result-loop counts; fixed sizes and
   159	the successful loop lemma are supporting progress only.

