+## 4. Adequacy and real-program pinning
+
+Status: the statement is full-domain, result-constraining, satisfiable, and
+mechanically pinned, even though it is not proved.
+
+### Plain-language claims
+
+The eight claims in [spec.k](/candidate/spec.k:9) state:
+
+| Claim | Precondition and asserted result |
+|---|---|
+| `inner-one-ahead` | At row `I`, with `0 <= J <= N` and the unique 1 at `(I,C)` with `J <= C`, executing the actual inner `while` ends at `j=N` and records the unique 1 coordinates. |
+| `inner-no-one` | If the unscanned suffix cannot contain the unique 1, the same inner loop reaches `j=N` while preserving the existing `row,col`. |
+| `outer-one-ahead` | If the outer scan has not passed the row containing 1, the actual outer loop scans to `i=N,j=N` and records its unique coordinates. |
+| `outer-one-past` | Once the scan has passed that row, it finishes all remaining rows while preserving the recorded coordinates. |
+| `scan-finish` | From the source-level initial `i=row=col=0`, `outerLoop` finds the unique 1, leaves `i=j=N`, and preserves an arbitrary statement tail. |
+| `neighbor-finish` | Starting `neighbor=N*N+1`, the exact four source conditionals leave it equal to `neighborMin`, the minimum of the in-bounds orthogonal neighbors. |
+| `result-loop-tail` | At the actual evaluated positive loop guard with remaining count `R>0`, prefix `A`, exact odd-tail/return/call continuation and heap object, execution reaches the return continuation and the updated heap sequence satisfies `finishRel(A,OUT,R,M,K)`. |
+| `minpath-full-contract` | Calling the exact bound `minPath` body for every valid permutation grid and positive `K` returns fresh reference 0, whose list is exactly the alternating length-`K` sequence described by `finishRel`. |
+
+### Domain and result adequacy
+
+`validPerm(P,N*N)` means the flattened sequence has length `N*N`, every member
+is in `1..N*N`, and no member repeats.  It is therefore exactly a permutation,
+not a sample or bounded family.  `gridRows(P,N)` constructs exactly `N` rows of
+length `N`.  The target quantifies arbitrary mathematical integers `N>=2` and
+`K>0`.  The explicit `oneRow` and `oneCol` bounds are logical consequences of
+the permutation premise; they do not narrow the source contract.
+
+`?OUT` is not free: the post-state heap binds reference 0 to `list(?OUT)`, and
+the `ensures` clause constrains it through `finishRel`.  For
+`R=(K-pyMod(K,2))/2`, `finishRel` recursively requires `R` copies of the pair
+`1,M`, then appends 1 iff `K` is odd.  Thus the output has exactly length `K`
+and the required values.  The result is neither tautological nor a one-way
+condition that permits arbitrary output.
+
+Every entry precondition is satisfiable.  Concrete witnesses for all eight
+claims are recorded in
+[stage4-witnesses.log](/audit-output/evidence/stage4-witnesses.log), generated by
+[adequacy_witness.py](/audit-output/evidence/adequacy_witness.py).  In
+particular, `N=2`, `P=[1,2,3,4]`, and `K=3` satisfies the target; substituting it
+into the claimed summary gives `[1,2,1]`, identical to both Python
+implementations.
+
+### Mechanical pinning
+
+The target does not execute an unconnected summary.  It calls `Name("minPath")`
+and binds that name to a closure with body `minPathBody` in
+[spec.k](/candidate/spec.k:205).  `minPathBody` is a syntax macro in
+[verification.k](/candidate/verification.k:392), not an operational shortcut.
+
+Using the fresh definition, I parsed regenerated `solution.mpy` to KAST, expanded
+`minPathBody`, and compared the constructor trees.  The module contains exactly
+one function named `minPath` with parameters `grid,k`; no macro name remains
+after expansion; and both normalized body trees have SHA-256
+`24abe13bafb3564368f38cb50b6fc94bddd01ecc0c74a21c4d120ab1847c2e9e`.
+Constructor equality is true.  See
+[pinning_check.py](/audit-output/evidence/pinning_check.py) and
+[stage4-pinning.log](/audit-output/evidence/stage4-pinning.log).  Together with
+trusted translator identity, this is the permitted constructor-level
+source-to-claim comparison.  The omitted module-loading step is semantically
+inert because the claim supplies the same function name, parameters, closure
+parent, and body.
+
+## 5. Rule-by-rule static soundness review
+
+Status: no false rule conclusion was found on the intended domain, but important
+proof-local mathematical lemmas are admitted rather than derived.  This matters
+both to the trust ledger and to the task-specific conditional provision.
+
+### Exhaustive inventory
+
+The complete line-oriented inventory is
+[stage5-rule-inventory-v3.log](/audit-output/evidence/stage5-rule-inventory-v3.log),
+generated by [rule_inventory.py](/audit-output/evidence/rule_inventory.py).  It
