+| `assert.k`, `comprehension.k`, `concrete.k`, `dict.k`, `float.k`, `iter.k`, `methods.k`, `range.k`, `set.k`, `sort.k`, `str.k`, `tuple.k` | 3, 7, 16, 28, 121, 0, 75, 6, 12, 19, 28, 21 | Exhaustively inventoried.  Their top-level operations are absent from `solution.mpy`; no rule in these groups provides a competing rewrite for the used program states.  Shared value constructors and helpers agree with the fixed model. |
+
+The program-to-rule map is preserved in
+[stage5-program-rule-map.log](/audit-output/evidence/stage5-program-rule-map.log).
+All used source constructors—`Module`, `FuncDef`, `Assign`, `Name`, `Int`,
+`Call`, `Attribute`, `ListExpr`, `Subscript`, `BinOp`, `Compare`, `If`, `While`,
+`Expr`, and `Return`—map to supplied declarations and operational rules.  The
